WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.020
[light music]

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:08.260
Testing is a crucial part of chiplet-based
systems, ensuring quality,

3
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:13.820
reliability, and cost efficiency at
every stage of the manufacturing process.

4
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.770
Advanced packaging has resulted

5
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.780
in increased challenges
in chiplet testability.

6
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.200
Chiplet testing happens at
multiple levels: wafer level,

7
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.580
die level,

8
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.540
and whole system package level.

9
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.860
Each step is designed to detect
defects, optimize yield,

10
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.540
and improve long-term reliability of
the product with the lowest escape rate.

11
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.350
First, substrate testing
ensures that the foundation

12
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.140
for chiplet integration is defect-free.

13
00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.450
This is done by using flying probe tests

14
00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.780
to detect open circuits
and shorts in interconnects.

15
00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:59.730
Next, wafer level sorting
and testing by automatic equipment is

16
00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.880
performed before the wafer is
diced into individual chiplets.

17
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.340
This includes probe tests, burn-in tests,

18
00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:11.680
and parametric analysis to measure
electrical characteristics.

19
00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.620
After dicing, chiplets
undergo die level testing.

20
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:20.920
This includes scan tests and functional
tests to identify known good dies,

21
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:25.440
or KGDs, that are free of defects
before they are packaged.

22
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.080
Once assembled into multi-chip
modules and then packages,

23
00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.060
chiplet systems undergo package
level testing and fault isolation.

24
00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:39.620
This ensures that all chiplets
are correctly connected,

25
00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.580
functional, and performing as expected.

26
00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.480
System level testing is the final step,

27
00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.620
validating the entire assembled
product in real world conditions.

28
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.860
This includes thermal, power,
and functional stress tests.

29
00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:58.640
Design for testability, or DFT
techniques, such as scan chains,

30
00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.680
boundary scan, and built-in
self-test or BIST,

31
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.240
help streamline testing
and improve fault detection.

32
00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.759
Standardized testing
protocols from IEEE and JEDEC,

33
00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:15.980
such as IEEE 1149.x for
boundary scan and IEEE

34
00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:19.680
1838 for 3D integrated circuits or ICs,

35
00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.680
ensure interoperability
and test reliability.

36
00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.990
Chiplet testing can significantly
reduce manufacturing costs as it ensures

37
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.910
that a broken chiplet or package does not
get assembled in a larger system where it

38
00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:39.520
leads to throwing out the entire assembly
and many good subcomponents with it.

39
00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.420
Testing ensures the long-term
reliability of semiconductor products.

40
00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.320
In this course, we will explore chiplet
testing methodologies, industry standards,

41
00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.940
and best practices for ensuring
high-quality chiplet-based systems.

42
00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:01.540
Let's continue our journey into the future
of chiplet manufacturing and testing.

43
00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:09.460
[light music]

